  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nIssued 250 AM MDT THU MAY 14 2026\nA large trough digging across the northwest is expected to \ncenter over our area on Sunday, continuing a significant cooling\ntrend that will drop daytime temperatures 10-15 degrees below \nnormal. The low center passage will bring considerably strong \nnorthwest wind gusts throughout the area on Sunday. Snow levels \nwill lower to about 3500-5000 feet on Sunday. The system is \nstill expected to bring a 30-50% chance of rain-snow showers \nover higher terrain of southwest/west-central ID. Afternoon \nthunderstorms are possible over the ID mountains as well. From \nMonday through Wednesday of next week, our area will mostly stay\nunder a dry west-northwest flow with temperatures trending up \nto near seasonal normals. Long-range guidance projects a large \nPacific ridge building into the region next Thursday, continuing\na warming trend.",
